<title>BELGIUM: Bruton says important to stick to EMU timetable.</title>
<headline>Bruton says important to stick to EMU timetable.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish Prime Minister John Bruton said on Tuesday that it was important for the European Union to stick top the timetable for economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a clear determination on behalf of member states,&quot; he said as he entered a meeting of European Union centrist leaders.  </p>
<p>He added that the German economy looked very strong.</p>
<p>Asked whether he thought an EMU delay was possible, Bruton said he didn't think so.</p>
<p>&quot;It is very important to stick to the timetable,&quot; Bruton told reporters.</p>
<p>Brussels Newsroom ++ 32 2 287 6800</p>
